# Test vectors ported from GaryHughes/crocofix (MIT License, Copyright (c) 2019 Gary Hughes).
# Source: libcrocofix_tests/. crocofix uses one TEST_CASE per file with SECTIONs; the SECTION is named in each note.
# BodyLength/CheckSum of every validate expect=ok and frame vector verified with python3.
#
# Not ported:
# - message_tests.cpp "decode a message containing a data field" / "... in two pieces" and
#   "encode a message containing a data field": RawData(89) value contains SOH, which cannot be written with |.
# - "decode a message with a data field that has no preceeding size field", "... non numeric previous field value",
#   "... does not have a traling field separator": depend on RawDataLength(93)/RawData(89) semantics that a plain
#   tag=value scan does not have; under parse_fields they are well-formed, so porting them as errors would be wrong.
# - second pieces of the split-message SECTIONs: they rely on decoder state carried over from the first piece.
# - "format checksum ..." SECTIONs: formatting of an integer, no byte checksum is computed.
# - session_tests.cpp "Invalid CheckSum", "Invalid BodyLength", "Missing BodyLength", "Wrong BeginString",
#   "Missing BeginString": messages are generated at run time with live SendingTime, no literal bytes to port.
# - field_tests.cpp, field_collection_tests.cpp, session_state_tests.cpp: no wire-format parsing.

